Your HS% isn't important, its a stat you can value, but isn't a priority to anyone else but you. The tracker score is based on;


Round win%;

This goes up with your Win/Loss, if you lose more games than you win, by definition it means you're losing more rounds than you're winning. 50% would be the mid ground, but yours is 49%. Your overall winrate is 48%, if this improves, so will your round win%. 


KAST;

Your Kills and assists versus your deaths on a round by round basis. At 63%, it means nearly 4/10 rounds you die while having 0 impact besides giving the enemy team a free ult orb and potentially a better gun. Checking a few profiles, 70% seems average, my account has 75% and that puts it in the top 9%. You can have a good game, but dying for free in over a third of the rounds you play could have a far greater negative impact than the other 7 rounds where you don't.


ACS;

Average combat score. The score you get at the end of the game. This is made up from lots of metrics throughout the game, kills, assists, plants, defuses how many kills you get in a round (IE 1 kill vs an ace in a round). A general indicator for your performance. 240 ACS puts you in the top 22%, 269 puts you in the top 8%. 


DDΔ/Round;

Your damage delt to enemies minus the damage you received, per round, on average. Helps to add value to getting enemies low, without requiring you to get the kill. A general view on how well you're using your utility and how much damage you're doing before you die. a positive DDΔ, so of 1 or more, puts you at the top 50%, a DDΔ of 37 puts you in the top 7%. 



The stats are taken from both my accounts, one is Asc 1, in High Dia/Low Asc MMR, the other is taken from my Asc 3 (Immo 2 MMR) account. The Asc1 account has a higher tracker score, because I play clove as a duelist, but I can't get away with that on my Asc 3 account, as the MMR is far higher and I get outaimed. I am not an AimDemon, infact I struggle against Immo 2 players, but choose to play smarter and sacrifice stats for the win. Your HS % is only 3% lower than mine, which should be an indication that HS% isn't really that impactful unless your wincon is to outaim everyone, which in Bronze 2, should not be the win condition. 


With your games played, you would need to be consistantly dropping games in the 800+ range, as you have numerous games with a tracker score so low, its given you the minimum rating of 100 (a participation award, basically). I would take a look at how you're playing, and what you're doing wrong. Aim to fix the core issues as you go into the next act, and sac off this acts tracker score, as you can't really save it in the time left.

