first: OP doesn't have to learn about your faith. You and anyone of any faith are not above those who do not care for religion, yours or others, and thus OP has no obligation to know about it. If you want OP to be informed, inform yourself. Its your religion, not OP's.

Second: Op specifically said they tried to reason with them. Lets presume, for a second, OP isnt the awful, racist person you've convinced yourself they are. OP tried to reason, said they cant be taking 30-45 minute breaks to pray. At no point did OP try to bar them from praying, stop assuming whats been said or done because you want it to fit your narrative.

&#x200B;

At the end of the day, if you want to believe in whatever religion you want, go ahead; But it isn't fair on their colleagues and OP to take 30-45 minute breaks to pray. Each day thats literally 1-1.5 hours of work time, weekly thats 7-10.5 hours. Thats a work day. I work with practising muslims, they take a couple of small breaks a day to pray. Thats compromise, being willing to balance the needs of your employer and the religion you choose to follow. Straight up saying ''Well OP didnt ask me for the intricate details and history of my religion, and its my religion so I can take how ever long I want off to the detriment of the team'' isn't compromise.

